{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox","id":1465611,"title":"Enchantment granting immunity to Paradox?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-28T01:14:58-07:00","id":1465611,"title":"Enchantment granting immunity to Paradox?","content":"Technomancers\u2019 Toybox has a Device called Doc Eon\u2019s Lemurian Lightning Gun, which is very vulgar but doesn\u2019t suffer Paradox due to its runes:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doc Eon\u2019s Lemurian Lightning Gun<br /> <br /> Arete 5, Quintessence unknown (see below), Background Cost N/A<br /> <br /> This odd weapon, shaped somewhat like an old dueling pistol, is ornately carved with Lemurian glyphs - the handwriting of the ancient civilization of Lemuria, whose only remnants survive among the Goro monks of the Hollow Earth. In place of a pan, the hammer strikes a red Mu Stone, which in turn ignites the sealed polarium container inside the gun, sending forth a bolt of lightning-like energy from the barrel. When the bolt hits its target, the blast is powerful enough to rend metal. Supposedly, this energy destroyed Lemuria in much the same way that many believe nuclear weapons will destroy the modern world. Because of its dangerous forces, Doc devised a dial that allows the gun to fire a limited stream, capable of stunning most people but not killing them.<br /> <br /> The \u201cignition source,\u201d polarium, is a enigmatic metal discovered in the North Pole, near the entrance of the Hollow Earth. Its properties, like Mu Stones, have not been fully studied, but the Lemurian containers - artifacts of an older time, now owned by the monks \u2014 are sealed airtight and seem to be indestructible. The Lightning Gun\u2019s most remarkable features, however, are its glyphs. According to Doc Eon\u2019s friend and biographer Joe \u201cLucky Skunk\u201d Ross, <b>the Lemurian runes made the Device immune to Paradox energies!</b> All attempts to replicate these mysterious sigils have failed, which leads the Etherites to conclude that some ancient Lemurian Science managed to overrule the most basic tenets of reality. As of yet, no one has managed to duplicate the feat (not to say that they haven\u2019t been trying...). The Goro monks themselves seem to have lost the secret; the glyphs were carved onto the Doc\u2019s gun by the last Lama to fully understand their significance.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the only two surviving Lightning Guns are pretty valuable. One supposedly rests in the Gernsback Continuum. I have no idea where the other might be. \u201cLucky Skunk\u201d would like to know where it is, though - supposedly, it once belonged to him.<br /> <br /> [<b>Although this Device is highly vulgar, its odd runes (which cannot be duplicated \u2014 sorry) make it immune to Paradox.</b> The \u201cArete\u201d roll unleashes a bolt of lightning that inflicts normal Forces damage. A \u201cmercy dial\u201d allows the user to tone the Effect down, reducing the damage by half. Nobody knows how many shots these guns are good for; the special combustion combination might make a pistol\u2019s energy supply effectively infinite, or it might be just about exhausted. Until the gun refuses to fire again, its limits remain a mystery. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t see similiar examples. Is this just a lone case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 10-28-2021, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:10:42-07:00","id":1465654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox#post1465611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven\u2019t see similiar examples. Is this just a lone case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is, that's why it doesn't have a stated cost and repeats so many times that it can't be replicated.<br /> <br /> Old artifacts that bend or break some rules are a staple of the game. They may have whatever significance or explanation the ST wants, as they are as much plot devices as they are items.<br /> <br /> Is there a secret Prime effect that can nullify Paradox? Is it the product of actual science that works on unknown Consensual laws? Is it the work of some lost Sphere or other ancient magical secret? Is it simply non-awakened magic? The answer, if ever possible to grasp, is up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T10:29:24-07:00","id":1465668,"title":"","content":"Nullifying Paradox is a Prime 5 effect, so I imagine that's ultimately what's behind it. But the effect as far as I understand is to safely nullify accumulated paradox, not to prevent it from accumulating in the first place.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the artifact you reference is unique. Also note that the end of the description gives the ST an out - the gun may become nothing more than a paperweight after firing it once. Or it might last forever. Totally in the hands of the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T11:04:14-07:00","id":1465673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox?p=1465668#post1465668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nullifying Paradox is a Prime 5 effect, so I imagine that's ultimately what's behind it. But the effect as far as I understand is to safely nullify accumulated paradox, not to prevent it from accumulating in the first place.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the artifact you reference is unique. Also note that the end of the description gives the ST an out - the gun may become nothing more than a paperweight after firing it once. Or it might last forever. Totally in the hands of the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I also think it\u2019s a special Prime 5 enchantment, each shot it works to nullify paradox, but this may not enough to make Sons of Ether curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T11:45:28-07:00","id":1465675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox?p=1465673#post1465673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I also think it\u2019s a special Prime 5 enchantment, each shot it works to nullify paradox, but this may not enough to make Sons of Ether curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Observe that the gun makes no roll for the Paradox Nullifying effect and have no limit on it. The gun is simply immune, no matter what, no matter when.<br /> <br /> I'd say that anything a Master needs more than 15 successes to make is worth of study. It can be simple to understand to us as players, but for the characters it is pretty impressive and nearly incomprehensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T08:37:24-07:00","id":1466129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox?p=1465675#post1465675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observe that the gun makes no roll for the Paradox Nullifying effect and have no limit on it. The gun is simply immune, no matter what, no matter when.<br /> <br /> I'd say that anything a Master needs more than 15 successes to make is worth of study. It can be simple to understand to us as players, but for the characters it is pretty impressive and nearly incomprehensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no roll for paradox nullification. It's 1 quint to 1 paradox nullified, which since with that level of prime you can generate quint from nothing.... And it would already need to do so to generate lightning from nothing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T17:11:34-08:00","id":1474061,"title":"","content":"I dislike how they say 'it can't be duplicated' instead of just sticking to 'so far nobody has been awesome enough to figure out how to duplicate it'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T17:53:00-08:00","id":1474064,"title":"","content":"A proper mage would take \u201ccan't be duplicated\u201d as a challenge\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T13:20:35-08:00","id":1474089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465611-enchantment-granting-immunity-to-paradox?p=1474064#post1474064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A proper mage would take \u201ccan't be duplicated\u201d as a challenge\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule, WOD hasn't hasn't liked Proper mages since the end of second edition. Powerful mages have the ability to straight-up ignore the setting's attempts at personal and cosmic horror as well as many of the core problems that keep starting mages from just, fixing things.<br /> <br /> Not that that's necessarily a bad thing. I miss how second used to lean into campy 90's action movie territory as much as the horror movie stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T03:24:13-08:00","id":1474115,"title":"","content":"Mind you that <b>&quot;Can't be duplicated&quot;</b> does not equal <b>&quot;Your Mage cannot create a wonder like this&quot;.</b><br /> It simply means <b>&quot;Your Mage cannot recreate this Wonder's mechanics with pure Sphere Magick alone.&quot;</b> Which is true: There is no way to create a Wonder like that - an obviously vulgar thing that simply ignores Paradox completely all the time - with Spheres alone.<br /> <br /> It does <i>not</i> mean that your Mage can't find ways to combine Sphere Magick with other components to be found in the WoD to recreate a wonder like that. We are talking about Doc Eon here. The Etherite that went onto so many glorious Otherworld adventures that he and his companions got their own in-game serialized novels about their hijinks.<br /> Perhaps he found an alien artifact that is secretly integrated into the thing. Maybe the wonder got blessed by some mystic guardian of some otherworldly realm that Doc Eon did a favor for. If there is any character who probably got their hands onto things like that through their very nature, it's him.<br /> <br /> Mage itself is chock-full of things that cannot be simply recreated without Paradox from the get-go: Many of the higher tiers of Merits work exactly along those lines, and are always explained by unknown or external influences, blessings or benefits. It's just that this Wonder has its own benevolent Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T08:35:33-08:00","id":1474127,"title":"","content":"Sphere Magic does so many things that many players seem to forget that even in Mage alone it isn't the whole of magical phenomena. Nightfolk have a plethora of their own powers and mystical artifacts, we must remember that explaining out vampires as Thaumivores is a common Hermetic <i>theory</i>, not a fact of the game. The fact of the game is that aliens, spirits, Nightfolk, bygones and many other things <u><b>are</b></u> supernatural and <b><u>aren't</u></b> Mages or subject to Paradox.<br /> <br /> Including such stuff into your wonders isn't really that much of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T00:06:52-08:00","id":1474168,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if this were a magical device in VtM or WtA or CtD nobody would be asking why it doesn't accrue Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}